<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Blood Death Knight Trinkets</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by what it is that you and your raid need. A Stamina trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105070/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> will make you the least likely to die, especially in a 25-player raiding environment, while a trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105111/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> will offer avoidance through the high Strength-to-Parry conversion, with some damage through the critical strike damage modifier, and active mitigation through the Haste &amp; Mastery modifier. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105134/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is by far your strongest offensive trinket. A skilled Death Knight will try to snapshot their diseases at the tail end of the trinket's proc effect for a nearly 100% crit snapshot. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a> also snapshots crit, meaning in an ideal world you would like to use both Dancing Rune Weapon and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a> for a double disease snapshot.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105111/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> - This is generally our second strongest offensive trinket, but in a fully offensive gear set up, it can outperform <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105134/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a>. It also brings some defensive utility as it amplifies both haste and mastery, in addition to buffing our critical strike damage.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105029/haromms-talisman">
<img alt="Haromm's Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haromm's Talisman</span></a> - Yes, we're back to including agility trinkets on our BIS lists. This trinket is great simply due to the Multistrike effect. Agility does give a very small amount of crit to a strength-based user, but this trinket should be prioritized to other agility users.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105147/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a> - Despite being a stamina trinket, it has quite strong offensive utility for the Blood Death Knight due to it lining up perfectly with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>. This is a perfect trinket for those looking for a more balanced trinket option.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104961/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> - This trinket is simply a niche trinket that excels in fights where there are a lot of targets for you to cleave. Bosses like Spoils and Galakras stand out as great fights for this trinket.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105070/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> - This is your strongest defensive trinket, reducing the cooldown of the following abilities by up to 17%: <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48792/icebound-fortitude">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_iceboundfortitude.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebound Fortitude</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49222/bone-shield">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_boneshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bone Shield</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55233/vampiric-blood">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_lifedrain.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vampiric Blood</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=48707/anti-magic-shell">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anti-Magic Shell</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104940/rooks-unlucky-talisman">
<img alt="Rook's Unlucky Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rook's Unlucky Talisman</span></a> - This trinket has incredible situational use due to its long duration and short cooldown. Of course, only a few things that are considered AOE are dangerous for tanks, but one clear example of where it shines is if you're looking to soak <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=144969/annihilate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/sha_spell_fire_bluehellfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Annihilate</span></a> during the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=71865/garrosh-hellscream">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Garrosh Hellscream</span></a> intermissions for additional <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105147/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a> - This trinket makes it on both the lists due to its strong defensive utility through stamina, and strong offensive utility through the crit on-use, which lines up perfectly with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49028/dancing-rune-weapon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dancing Rune Weapon</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105016/juggernauts-focusing-crystal">
<img alt="Juggernaut's Focusing Crystal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_19.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Focusing Crystal</span></a> - This trinket turns all of your offensive abilities into a small heal on yourself. In practice, the healing is quite neglicable, and offers limited utility outside of a few circumstances.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Blood Death Knights</span></h2>With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
