<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<b>Defensive Option</b></div></td>
<td>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<b>Offensive Option</b></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As with the <span class="q5">legendary meta gem</span>, we have access to both an offensive and defensive option when it comes to the legendary cloaks. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Which should you use? </b>Well, the answer is not black and white. As you head into Siege of Orgimmar progression, most people should default to <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> operates as a cheat death with a 2-minute cooldown. It's quite unique in the way that it functions, however. If you have 90% health, take a massive swing that would've killed you; the cloak will absorb the entire hit, leaving you at 90% health after the cloak procs. On the flip side, if you are tanking many small adds and have 2% health before taking a fatal hit, the cloak will put you back at 2% health, which will likely not save you from dying. If you do happen to die while the effect of the cloak is on cooldown, the cooldown will be cleared when you resurrect.  <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> procs a continuous frontal cleave approximately two times per minute. This effect scales with Attack Power from <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> and is responsible for approximately 5% of your overall damage on single target encounters. Where this effect shines is on encounters where cleave damage is valued or where you are very unlikely to make use of the cheat death effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>This cloak should be used to great effect while farming celestial dungeons.<div class="box" data-level="null">
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<b>
<span class="c6">Special Note for Death Knights</span></b></div>
<br/>Early in the original Mists of Pandaria cycle, the effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> was proccing at the same time as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114556/purgatory">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_shadowegg.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purgatory</span></a>, making it essentially useless. However, on the version of the game we're playing right now, the effect from the cloak will always proc <b>before</b> Purgatory, making you have two separate cheat deaths as a Death Knight.</div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Blood Death Knight</span></h2>Crafted items are, for the most part, no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Blacksmith, for example, you can still equip anything Blacksmiths craft. <br/>
<br/>A few of the crafted pieces will be part of your Best-in-Slot set before you step into raid.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98607/avengers-trillium-legplates">
<img alt="Avenger's Trillium Legplates" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_40v3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenger's Trillium Legplates</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98616/avengers-trillium-waistplate">
<img alt="Avenger's Trillium Waistplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_93v3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenger's Trillium Waistplate</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98606/protectors-trillium-legguards">
<img alt="Protector's Trillium Legguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Trillium Legguards</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98615/protectors-trillium-waistguard">
<img alt="Protector's Trillium Waistguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Trillium Waistguard</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94265/haunted-steel-treads">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Treads</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94266/haunted-steel-greathelm">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greathelm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greathelm</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94267/haunted-steel-warboots">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Warboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Warboots</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94268/haunted-steel-headguard">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Headguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Headguard</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Blood Death Knights</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 7.5% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed. In terms of actual rating, you need <b>2550 Hit</b> and <b>2550 Expertise</b> to reach these caps before accounting for racial bonuses.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might. <br/>
<br/>Reaching 7.5% Hit, otherwise referred to as the "Hit cap," will not guarantee that your spells, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=108196/death-siphon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_deathknight_deathsiphon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Siphon</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=77575/outbreak">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathvortex.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Outbreak</span></a> will land. For that, you'll need Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. A lot of bosses have mechanics that make them unable to parry. Important spells, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=49998/death-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_butcher2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Strike</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=62036/rune-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_darkconviction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rune Strike</span></a>, cannot be parried, so reaching 15% Expertise to reach the "hard cap" becomes quite unnecessary. <br/>
<br/>For classes with spells like the Death Knight, reaching this 7.5% number will guarantee your spells land.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c6" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Blood Death Knights</span></h2>Your gems will alternate depending on what you and your raid prioritize. We generally have 3 different playstyles (<i>Offensive</i>, <i>Balanced</i>, and <i>Defensive</i>), and below you'll find the appropriate gems for each playstyle. We generally opt to socket for the socket bonus, but if the bonus does not offer an attractive bonus, then opt for the<b> main gem</b> of each category. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<span class="q5">Legendary Meta Gem:</span></b> In Phase 3 of Mists of Pandaria, we get access to two new meta gems that provide far greater utility than the normal meta gems. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> are the two we can realistically use, and for most people, it should not be much of a choice. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> provides the most utility overall with an outrageously high uptime, north of 50%. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> does scale with Vengeance and generally provides a 5-6% damage boost. <br/>
<br/>
